  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengtening Youth Policy Through Partnership in</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In response to Jordan&#x2019;s evolving economic and social landscape, UNICEF with the Ministry of Youth (MoY) proposes to launch a National Youth Survey 2025, followed by the development of the National Youth Strategy 2026&#x2013;2030. Alongside core funding, &#xa0;USAID and Netherlands funding, Ireland&#x2019;s support of &#x20ac;130,000 will enable these activities, which aim to inform evidence-based policymaking, aligned with Jordan&#x2019;s EMV, PSMR and Sustainable Development Goal commitments. The new strategy will serve as a comprehensive roadmap to advance youth well-being, empowerment, and inclusion. It will integrate cross-cutting priorities, including innovation, digital access, green growth, equity and inclusion, mental health and wellbeing, peace and security, and social cohesion</narrative>
  </description>
